{
  "id": "principle-of-common-fate",
  "term": "principle of common fate",
  "definition": "The principle of common fate is a Gestalt grouping idea in vision: elements that move in the same way are perceived as belonging together, such as forming one contour or texture region. It describes how shared motion can shape how visual form is organized.",
